   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Dear prof. Jorgensen,<div><br></div><div>In the situation above, how can we tell whether metric invariance is achieved across several groups with just-identified models? Do we use CFI = 1.000 for comparing with the CFI from the metric model (calculating delta CFI), or do we just interpret the CFI of the metric model (e.g., if CFI &gt; .95, metric variance is achieved)?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you,</div><div>Dominik<br><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
